It is difficult to know where to draw the line between death and war in 
some cases. I divided it by picking War as a straight 'kill something as 
might be common in a war'. It should indeed include fists and attack 
spells (but not wands). It would be better yet though to find a better 
scoring for War. I just can't think of it.

Why don't you think pacifists should be Death? To me it makes by far the 
most sense; they cause a great deal of death through means unaccountable 
by war, disease, or hunger. They could still become famine fairly 
easily; don't forget about the negative death points for healing pets.

Not all conduct types should have equal chance of each rider. Avoiding 
some extreme/repetitive behaviors it should be fairly easy to pick your 
own rider if you want. I believe the best way to do this is to have a 
LARGE list of things to gain and lose points for. The more ideas the better.


